 "format": "rustsheet-case/v1",
 "description": "T-4634: which data-field mix switches a 2-D pivot Sum total from the child cells to the records, and the order of grand totals. E1-E12 (27 records each, R first seen Q X B, K first seen M Z A, three per cell) are searched with Python doubles so that every row and column total's cell sum (display order) differs from its item-by-item record accumulation, and the grand-grand candidates separate. S1 Sum alone; X1-X12 Sum beside Count, CountNums, Max, Min, Product, StdDev, Var, Varp, StdDevp, Average (X10-X12); A1 Average alone. F1/F2: Sum alone (O1-O4) and Average alone (A2, A3) over one axis field, separating the item cells, item-by-item and record order. G1/G2 (36 records, values 800-1300 so that rounding differences are amplified): Var, Varp and StdDevp 2-D (V1-V3, V6, V7) and Varp over one field (V4, V5). H1 (32 records): rows P, Q and columns U, W; T1 Sum alone, T2 Sum beside Average, T3 Average alone, separating 17 orders of subtotal-by-subtotal cells. ER: t4616 D3; C1-C7 Count or CountNums of Err beside only Max, Min, Product, Var, Varp or StdDev of Num. Candidate values are in docs/excel-semantics/pivots.md. Pivot cells are in the sidecar's `pivots` section; Q!A1 makes the case scored.",
